# SQLite scratch databases. ``data/`` is the conventional home for these, but a
# database created anywhere else (a service directory, a repo-root probe) must
# not become committable by accident -- these files hold audit trails, user
# records and ticket content.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
*.db

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Claude Code's per-project state. ``.claude/settings.local.json`` holds local
# permission grants and is machine-specific. It happens to be covered by a
# global ignore on the machine this repo was developed on
# (``~/.config/git/ignore``), but that file does not travel with the repository
# -- on a collaborator's checkout or in CI it is absent, and this directory
# would silently become committable. Ignore it here so the protection is part of
# the repo rather than part of one developer's machine.
.claude/

# Working design document, deliberately not a repository deliverable. It is the
# "二次开发方案" written against baseline b08da7f -- a planning artefact for the
# Phase 1-4 build, not something the finished repo ships. Ignored rather than
# merely left untracked so that a later ``git add -A`` cannot sweep it in by
# accident: the decision not to publish it is enforced by the repo, not by
# whoever happens to be typing the commit.
analysis_plan.md

# NOTE: ``app/static/react/`` is the Vite ``outDir`` (see vite.config.js) and its
# build output IS committed -- that is how the container and a fresh checkout
# serve the UI without running Node. Run ``npm run build`` and commit the
# regenerated ``index.html`` together with the new hashed files under
# ``app/static/react/assets/``; committing index.html alone points the page at
# files that are not in the repository. The old ``frontend/dist/`` rule here was
# dead -- Vite never wrote there.
